  "record_type": "completed_distribution_specific_velocity_sector_audit",
  "scientific_conclusion": "The fixed Stage-115 comparison finds shared adjacent angular support rather than a single-sector mechanism. In the near-wall band, sectors 5+6 carry 65.1031% of phi and 59.3056% of psi; in the mid band they carry 58.1059% and 53.5985%, respectively. Phi/psi profile cosine similarity remains 0.990319 near the wall and 0.986807 in the mid band, with overlap coefficients 0.922590 and 0.913739. This is a positive localization result for a common adjacent pair, not evidence of limiter causality, MUSCL stability, endpoint convergence, heat-flux improvement, benchmark accuracy, or validation. The preregistered next route is the fixed pair-resolved radial-node audit; no velocity quadrature or failed physical/numerical parameter is retuned.",
